── FACT BEYOND A `without` LIMIT ──── E0204_one_line_one_mistake.lt:4:3  [E0204]

`List.map` allocates, through `List.new`, but `labels` says `without alloc`:

  3 │ pub fn labels(prices: List<Price>) -> List<str> without alloc {
    │                                                         ───── the limit
  4 │   prices.map(|p| "{p.cents}")
    │   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    │              ─────────────── also allocates
    │                  ─────────── also allocates
    │                    ─────── also allocates

Code under `without alloc` makes no list or string. Let the caller make it, and
take it `inout`: writes through its indexes stay in its storage, as `out[i] = x`
does.
